{
  "about": "The centre of the visualizer look, different per video: 10 palettes (in 7 colour families: two videos in a row never share one) x 7 ring shapes x 3 particle styles = 210 combinations. Pairwise coprime sizes, so the least recently used item on each axis (ties: the order here) walks through all 210 before one repeats; the palettes are ordered so that two of one family stay five apart. `overrides` are m10-visualizer preset keys (presets/m10.yaml); every shape keeps the ring's farthest bar tip within the default preset's, so the side column drawn at S3 stays clear. Read by scripts/rcvlib/center.py; references/design_notes.md explains the rules.",
